1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:01,300
Got this tendon?

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:01,855
Touch your thumb

3
00:00:01,855 --> 00:00:02,635
to your pinky

4
00:00:02,635 --> 00:00:04,460
and bend your wrist.

5
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,428
That cord's a muscle

6
00:00:05,428 --> 00:00:07,600
your body forgot to delete.

7
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:09,550
One in seven of us?

8
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:10,933
Already deleted...

9
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,100
sometimes in just one arm.

10
00:00:13,137 --> 00:00:14,137
It probably helped

11
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:15,585
our tree-climbing ancestors

12
00:00:15,585 --> 00:00:16,767
hang on.

13
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:17,457
Today?

14
00:00:17,457 --> 00:00:18,807
You grip just as hard

15
00:00:18,807 --> 00:00:19,940
without it.

16
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:21,933
So surgeons take it out...

17
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:23,184
and use it to rebuild

18
00:00:23,184 --> 00:00:25,689
baseball pitchers' elbows.

19
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:26,990
No cord?

20
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:28,444
Check your other arm.

21
00:00:28,490 --> 00:00:29,950
Or ask a baseball

22
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:31,164
PITCHER.

